hat are easy to identify in campaign performance reports (If you are using the Similarweb platform you can create user-friendly tags to track your Google Analytics performance better). Below is a listing of each parameter: Website URL * : This is the target destination/the site that the link refers traffic to Campaign Source (UTM_source) * : A reference to where the link is placed for a potential visitor to click and be transported to your website (examples include a newsletter, Google ad, Facebook page, LinkedIn ad, blog site, etc.) Campaign Medium (UTM_medium) * : The channel of communication used for the link to your website (e.g., email, banner, CPC, social) Campaign Name (UTM_name): * : The name of the marketing campaign you’re running (e.g., custom_marketing_templates) Campaign Term (UTM_term) : Optional parameter that can be used to make the link specific to a keyword (e.g., for differentiation when running paid search ads) Campaign Content (UTM_content) : An optional parameter used for tracking A/B test variants How to use the free UTM Builder Just fill out the relevant fields with the needed info. Start with the website address, and then fill out your campaign details in the \"Source\", \"Medium\", \"Name\" fields, etc. Now all you have to do is click \"Copy link\" and you have your free UTM code, ready for tracking. Enjoy! Follow us on: Derech Yitzhak Rabin 33, Givatayim, 5348303, Israel Get our free extension Rankings Top Websites Top Android Apps Top iOS Apps Top Amazon Products & Brands Digital 100 Mobile vs. Desktop Free Tools Website Traffic Checker AI Traffic Checker Free App Analytics Keyword Generator SERP Seismometer Solutions Enterprise Web Intelligence App Intelligence Retail Intelligence Sales Intelligence Stock Intelligence Data-as-a-Service Advisory Services Custom Reporting Data Our Data Verify Your Website Browser Extension Resources Blog Reports Webinars Events Knowledge Center & Support Insights About us Company Partners Customers Leaders